From: rhodep port <none@example.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 14:45:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] DIAGNOSTIC: net: ipa: unmask and report the error interrupts

Not for source= beyond the investigation it belongs to.

ipa_interrupt_process() handles UC_0, UC_1 and TX_SUSPEND and sends
everything else to "silently ignore (and clear) any other condition".
Nothing ever unmasks the error conditions either, so BAD_SNOC_ACCESS,
RX_ERR, DEAGGR_ERR, TX_ERR, PROC_ERR and TX_HOLB_DROP cannot be seen at
all.

The reset being chased takes the SoC down with no CPU exception, no
backtrace and no SMMU fault, seconds after the modem registers on the
network with IPA loaded. An access the interconnect refuses is one of the
few things that looks like that from outside, and BAD_SNOC_ACCESS is
exactly how IPA reports one from inside.

Unmask them and name whichever arrives.

Signed-off-by: rhodep port <none@example.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ipa/ipa_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ipa/ipa_main.c
@@ -154,6 +154,20 @@
 
 	ipa->setup_complete = true;
 
+	/*
+	 * DIAGNOSTIC: the error conditions IPA can raise are never unmasked,
+	 * so ipa_interrupt_process() only ever sees them as "any other
+	 * condition" and clears them without a word. BAD_SNOC_ACCESS in
+	 * particular is what an access the interconnect refuses looks like
+	 * from in here, and that is the shape of the reset being chased.
+	 */
+	ipa_interrupt_enable(ipa, IPA_IRQ_BAD_SNOC_ACCESS);
+	ipa_interrupt_enable(ipa, IPA_IRQ_RX_ERR);
+	ipa_interrupt_enable(ipa, IPA_IRQ_DEAGGR_ERR);
+	ipa_interrupt_enable(ipa, IPA_IRQ_TX_ERR);
+	ipa_interrupt_enable(ipa, IPA_IRQ_PROC_ERR);
+	ipa_interrupt_enable(ipa, IPA_IRQ_TX_HOLB_DROP);
+
 	dev_info(dev, "IPA driver setup completed successfully\n");
 
 	return 0;
--- a/drivers/net/ipa/ipa_interrupt.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ipa/ipa_interrupt.c
@@ -100,7 +100,16 @@
 		ipa_interrupt_suspend_clear_all(interrupt);
 		fallthrough;
 
-	default:	/* Silently ignore (and clear) any other condition */
+	default:	/* DIAGNOSTIC: say which one, then clear as before */
+		dev_err_ratelimited(ipa->dev,
+				    "IPA interrupt %u (%s)\n", irq_id,
+				    irq_id == IPA_IRQ_BAD_SNOC_ACCESS ? "BAD_SNOC_ACCESS" :
+				    irq_id == IPA_IRQ_RX_ERR	     ? "RX_ERR" :
+				    irq_id == IPA_IRQ_DEAGGR_ERR     ? "DEAGGR_ERR" :
+				    irq_id == IPA_IRQ_TX_ERR	     ? "TX_ERR" :
+				    irq_id == IPA_IRQ_PROC_ERR	     ? "PROC_ERR" :
+				    irq_id == IPA_IRQ_TX_HOLB_DROP   ? "TX_HOLB_DROP" :
+				    irq_id == IPA_IRQ_GSI_EE	     ? "GSI_EE" : "other");
 		iowrite32(mask, ipa->reg_virt + offset);
 		break;
 	}
